#### Solution:
This program uses a loop to reverse the order of the letters in a word. It first stores the entire word into a character array using `toCharArray()`. Then it loops through all the elements of the array from right to left. For every element, it prints out the character at the current index position. Since we start our iteration from the last element, we decrement the value of `i` after printing the character so that the next time around the loop, the previous character gets printed before the present one.

